course: dictionary
lesson: 12899
title: Equivalent: the same amount, or the same meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Equivalent means equal. Two things are equivalent when they have the same value, amount, meaning or importance, even if they look different. «One half is equivalent to two quarters.» The numbers look different, but both name the same amount of pizza.
explain: In maths you will meet equivalent fractions, such as 1/2, 2/4 and 50/100. You will also meet equivalent measures. «One metre is equivalent to 100 centimetres.» Both say the same length, just in different units.
explain: The word is useful outside maths too. «The French equivalent of "hello" is "bonjour".» Here equivalent means the word that matches the meaning in another language. When you read it, ask: are these the same amount, or the same meaning? If yes, they are equivalent.
fact: Equivalent means equal in value, amount, meaning or importance.
fact: Equivalent can be an adjective: «These two fractions are equivalent.»
fact: An equivalent is a noun: something that equals or matches something else.
fact: «1/2 is equivalent to 2/4» because both fractions name the same amount.
fact: Useful phrases: equivalent to, equivalent fractions, the equivalent of.
exercise: Which fraction is equivalent to 1/2? | 1/3 | *2/4 | 1/4 | 2/3
exercise: «1 metre is equivalent to how many centimetres?» | *100 | 50 | 1000 | 10
exercise: Which word is an equivalent of «big» in meaning? | *large | quick | soft | small
test: Which pair shows equivalent fractions? | 1/3 and 1/4 | 4/5 and 5/4 | *3/6 and 1/2 | 2/5 and 3/5
test: Which word is the equivalent of «happy» in meaning? | angry | tired | sad | *glad
exam: Which amount is equivalent to 2 metres? | *200 centimetres | 20 centimetres | 200 millimetres | 2000 centimetres
